      "description": "Process an asset whose `classification.status` is `failed` again. It returns to `processing` and is moderated like a new upload. The moderation decision must still be pending and the asset must not be under a safety hold. Processing needs available file content, inline text, or an eligible website URL to load again.",
      "names": {
        "javascript": "assets.retry",
        "python": "assets.retry",
        "go": "Assets.Retry",
        "rust": "assets().retry",
        "java": "assets.retry",
        "ruby": "assets.retry",
        "php": "assets->retry"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "assets.explain",
      "kind": "method",
      "description": "Complete the policy evidence behind an asset's moderation decision. To decide quickly, moderation skips questions whose answers could not change any action, so a report marked `policy.evidence: \"decision\"` can credit a different rule, or show a different policy score, than a complete report would. Explaining answers those questions for the same content and returns the asset with `policy.evidence: \"full\"`; every action stays as decided. A decision made under policy settings that have since changed can't be explained as made: re-run it with `rerun: true` instead.",
      "names": {
        "javascript": "assets.explain",
        "python": "assets.explain",
        "go": "Assets.Explain",
        "rust": "assets().explain",
        "java": "assets.explain",
        "ruby": "assets.explain",
        "php": "assets->explain"
      }
    },
